block_snippets.snippet:
:::callout{kind=warning title="Data caveat"}
Reporting completeness was 62% this quarter.
:::

:::tiles{cols=3}
:::card{title="ANC4"}
Coverage rose 4pp.
:::
:::card{title="Deliveries"}
Flat against last year.
:::
:::card{title="PNC"}
Still the weakest link.
:::
:::

:::quote{cite="Dr N. Kamara, DHMT"}
The data finally matches what we see in the facilities.
:::

:::page{layout=story kicker="Place or programme"}
:::slot{name=side}
## Story headline
:::
Open with the situation before the change: what was not working, for whom, and how the numbers showed it.

Then say what was done about it: who acted, what they changed and when, in plain words a reader outside the programme can follow.

Close with what changed in the data and what it meant on the ground, with the number that shows it.
:::slot{name=media}
:::
:::

surface_css:
:root .fm-live-scope { background: var(--forge-surface-2, #f2f2f2); }
/* The EDITOR is the sheet: the printed sheet at 96dpi (the host sets
   --fm-sheet, 794px for A4, and --fm-measure so the column below is the
   printed column, 1:1, so lines wrap here exactly as they wrap in print),
   centered on the ground. Capping the editor element itself, not just its
   scroller, keeps the ground beside the sheet outside CodeMirror: a click
   there lands on the pane, not on the document. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-editor {
  background: transparent;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: var(--fm-sheet, 896px);
  margin-inline: auto;
}
/* CodeMirror's dotted focus outline would ring the whole sheet. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-editor.cm-focused { outline: none; }
/* The scroller paints the page ground. It must live HERE and not on
   .cm-content: the box layer draws at negative z, and an in-flow element's
   background would paint OVER it — a scroller's own background paints below
   its negative-z children. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-scroller {
  background: var(--fm-page);
  /* The sheet's edge on the pane's base-200: a hairline in the app's border
     colour, as a slide deck frames its slides, and no drop shadow. INSET and
     on the sides only: the sheet runs the pane's full height, and a seam's
     gap (.fm-page-gutter__band, an in-flow child) paints over an inset
     shadow, so each sheet's side edges stop at the gap instead of running
     on through it. */
  box-shadow: inset 1px 0 0 var(--forge-surface-3, #d9d9d9),
    inset -1px 0 0 var(--forge-surface-3, #d9d9d9);
  /* The scroller is a flex item: without an explicit width it would shrink
     to fit content. */
  width: 100%;
  /* The centering theme pads the scroller right to align the column past the
     app's floating sidebar. On the SHEET that padding would shrink the content
     area and paint the ground under the sidebar — neutralise it and take the
     same final position by shifting the centred sheet left by half the pad
     (the host mirrors the pad into --fm-center-pad). */
  padding-right: 0 !important;
  position: relative;
  left: calc(var(--fm-center-pad, 0px) / -2);
}
/* CodeMirror puts a zero-width <img class="cm-widgetBuffer"> beside every
   inline widget (its fix for Chrome's cursor placement). A replaced box is
   laid out by its own margin box, and at CodeMirror's vertical-align of
   text-top its top sits at the font's content-area top, which is ABOVE the
   strut whenever the line's line-height is tighter than that content area:
   every heading line (line-height 1.2) then stands up to 2px taller than
   print's heading, and the rest of the page follows it down. Aligned to the
   line box instead, the buffer keeps its place in the flow (and its purpose)
   and can never grow the line. Prose lines were never affected, their
   line-height being the looser of the two. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-widgetBuffer { vertical-align: top; }
/* The app sets tabular numerals on html/body/#app for its data tables; they
   inherit into the live preview, where print has proportional figures. In a
   font with both sets (every theme with a web font) that makes any line with
   digits measurably wider in Edit than in print, and it wraps a line early.
   The seam's footer and the contents page numbers set tabular-nums again for
   themselves, as the paged sheet does for print's margin boxes. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-content { font-variant-numeric: normal; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-content {
  background: transparent;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 100%;
  /* The base editor theme caps the writing column at 56rem; on the sheet the
     column is the measure, owned by the padding formula below — a wide/full
     document must outgrow that cap. */
  max-width: none;
  /* View's bleed-pad formula, with the sheet standing in for the viewport:
     % resolves against the scroller, so narrow windows match View too. The
     column is therefore --fm-measure less 48px; the host sets the var
     accordingly. */
  padding: 0 max(24px, calc((100% - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 + 24px)) 4rem;
}
/* With page boxes drawn the sheet ENDS at the last page's foot. The pad above
   is a flowing surface's room to scroll past its last line; under page boxes
   it is a strip of paper below the last page's bottom edge, which reads as
   the document running on past its own end. The class is on the SCROLLER
   while a pagination has pages (pageBoxPlugin, which explains why it may not
   be on the content). */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-scroller.cm-fm-paged .cm-content { padding-bottom: 0; }
/* No line insets: the base theme's 6px/2px would narrow the text by 8px
   against print, and against the rendered blocks beside it. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line { padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; }
/* An aligned paragraph's source lines, as print aligns the paragraph: each
   source line is a line break in print, so a justified line's last row
   stays ragged in both. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-align-left { text-align: left; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-align-center { text-align: center; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-align-right { text-align: right; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-align-justify { text-align: justify; }
/* buildFastrReportCss neutralises all bleed under a scope (a picker tile has
   no page to bleed into). The editor DOES have a page — the sheet — so these
   later rules re-aim the two bleed properties at the sheet's edges: a band or
   cover runs edge to edge of the sheet and its text returns to the measure,
   View's exact geometry with the sheet standing in for the viewport. */
:root .fm-live-scope {
  --fm-bleed-margin: calc((var(--fm-measure) - var(--fm-sheet, 896px)) / 2 - 24px);
  --fm-bleed-pad: calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 + 24px);
}
/* A cover's height is print's: 34rem at the 16px root, in px so the editor
   and the layout frame agree whatever their roots and viewports (the screen
   sheet's 72vh cap would make it depend on the window). With fill=page it
   fills its page: the host sets --fm-page-h to the printed page's height. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-cover { min-height: 544px; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-cover.fm-cover--fill { min-height: var(--fm-page-h, 544px); }
/* A page template is its page: a ground it takes is the whole sheet's, as
   print paints it (the runner's afterPageLayout), drawn here as shadows out
   to the sheet's edges (the widget's own overflow clips everything else). */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl.fm-tpl { --fm-tpl-pad: 0; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl.fm-tone--paper { box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-paper-ground), calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px)) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-paper-ground), calc(-1 * calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px))) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-paper-ground); }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl.fm-tone--ink { box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-ink-ground), calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px)) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-ink-ground), calc(-1 * calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px))) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-ink-ground); }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl.fm-tone--accent { box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-accent-ground), calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px)) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-accent-ground), calc(-1 * calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px))) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-accent-ground); }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl.fm-tone--warm { box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-warm-ground), calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px)) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-warm-ground), calc(-1 * calc((var(--fm-sheet, 896px) - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 - var(--fm-page-margin, 0px))) 0 0 var(--fm-page-margin, 0px) var(--fm-warm-ground); }
/* The page's margins, which the editor draws in its seams: painted with the
   ground of a page template that takes the page, the footer in its ink. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter.fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="paper"] {
  background: linear-gradient(var(--fm-paper-ground), var(--fm-paper-ground)) top / 100% calc(var(--fm-seam-fill, 0px) + var(--fm-page-margin, 77px)) no-repeat;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="paper"] .fm-page-gutter__foot {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-paper-ground-ink) 72%, transparent);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-start-ground="paper"] .fm-page-gutter__head,
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-head[data-start-ground="paper"] .fm-page-gutter__head {
  background: var(--fm-paper-ground);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter.fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="ink"] {
  background: linear-gradient(var(--fm-ink-ground), var(--fm-ink-ground)) top / 100% calc(var(--fm-seam-fill, 0px) + var(--fm-page-margin, 77px)) no-repeat;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="ink"] .fm-page-gutter__foot {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-ink-ground-ink) 72%, transparent);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-start-ground="ink"] .fm-page-gutter__head,
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-head[data-start-ground="ink"] .fm-page-gutter__head {
  background: var(--fm-ink-ground);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter.fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="accent"] {
  background: linear-gradient(var(--fm-accent-ground), var(--fm-accent-ground)) top / 100% calc(var(--fm-seam-fill, 0px) + var(--fm-page-margin, 77px)) no-repeat;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="accent"] .fm-page-gutter__foot {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent-ground-ink) 72%, transparent);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-start-ground="accent"] .fm-page-gutter__head,
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-head[data-start-ground="accent"] .fm-page-gutter__head {
  background: var(--fm-accent-ground);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter.fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="warm"] {
  background: linear-gradient(var(--fm-warm-ground), var(--fm-warm-ground)) top / 100% calc(var(--fm-seam-fill, 0px) + var(--fm-page-margin, 77px)) no-repeat;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-end-ground="warm"] .fm-page-gutter__foot {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-warm-ground-ink) 72%, transparent);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter[data-start-ground="warm"] .fm-page-gutter__head,
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-head[data-start-ground="warm"] .fm-page-gutter__head {
  background: var(--fm-warm-ground);
}
/* An empty photo slot: where the author adds one (print leaves it out). */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl-slot--empty.fm-tpl-slot--media {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-height: 9em;
  border: 2px dashed var(--fm-border);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  cursor: pointer;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl-slot--empty.fm-tpl-slot--media::after {
  content: "Add a photo";
}
/* An area holding more than it shows: hatched at its foot. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl .is-overfull { position: relative; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl .is-overfull::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  height: 1.6em;
  background: repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-danger) 55%, transparent) 0 0.35em, transparent 0.35em 0.7em);
}
/* Any other empty area: a dashed box to fill (print leaves it out). Text
   areas hold a ghost line to type on; the rest start on a press and say
   what they take. In the area's own ink, so it reads on any ground. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl > .fm-tpl-slot--empty:not(.fm-tpl-slot--media) {
  display: block;
  min-height: 3.2em;
  padding: 0.5em 0.7em;
  border: 1.5px dashed color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 35%, transparent);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl > .fm-tpl-slot--empty[data-fm-placeholder]:not(:has(.cm-fm-slot-ghost)) { display: grid; place-items: center; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl > .fm-tpl-slot--start { cursor: pointer; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-tpl > .fm-tpl-slot--empty[data-fm-placeholder]:not(:has(.cm-fm-slot-ghost))::after {
  content: attr(data-fm-placeholder);
  color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 60%, transparent);
  font-size: 0.85em;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-slot-ghost { margin: 0; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-slot-ghost:empty::before { color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent); }
/* With the caret in a template, each area is outlined: the toolbar names
   the one the caret is in. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region--active .fm-tpl > .fm-tpl-main,
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region--active .fm-tpl > .fm-tpl-slot:not(.fm-tpl-slot--empty) {
  outline: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent) 45%, transparent);
  outline-offset: -1px;
}

:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-h1 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-h1-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: var(--fm-h1-size);
  line-height: var(--fm-h1-line-height);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-h2 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-h2-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: var(--fm-h2-size);
  line-height: var(--fm-h2-line-height);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-h3 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-h3-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: var(--fm-h3-size);
  line-height: var(--fm-h3-line-height);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-h4 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-h4-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: var(--fm-h4-size);
  line-height: var(--fm-h4-line-height);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-h5 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-h5-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: var(--fm-h5-size);
  line-height: var(--fm-h5-line-height);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-h6 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-h6-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: var(--fm-h6-size);
  line-height: var(--fm-h6-line-height);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-code {
  font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 0.9em;
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: 0.05em 0.3em;
}
/* The markdown highlight style underlines anything Lezer tokenizes as a
   link — including bare [bracketed text] the renderer leaves literal. Only
   REAL links (given cm-fm-link by the conceal layer) may underline. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line * { text-decoration: none; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line .cm-fm-link, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-link {
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 2px;
}
/* A list line's marker sits in the indent the line's padding makes, as
   print's li::before does; the depth (from the source's indentation) is the
   number of indents. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-bullet { position: absolute; left: calc(var(--fm-li-indent, 1.4em) * (var(--fm-li-depth, 1) - 1)); width: var(--fm-li-indent, 1.4em); color: var(--fm-ink); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-bullet--glyph::before { content: var(--fm-bullet, "\2022"); }
/* A revealed region keeps LOOKING like the block while its source is edited:
   the lines carry the block's ground (a tone class, a callout accent, or the
   default surface wash) and the fence lines drop to dimmed syntax. Only
   layout-free sheet classes are reused per line — never the structural block
   classes, whose margins would repeat on every line. */
/* The revealed box model: the LAYER draws each block's box with the block's
   real sheet classes (borders, radius, shadow — the preview's own look); the
   lines only inset their text into it. Backgrounds live on the box, not the
   lines, so nothing ever paints over a border. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-revealed-first { padding-top: 0.35rem; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-revealed-last { padding-bottom: 0.35rem; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d1, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d2, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d3, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d4 { padding-inline: 0.9rem; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d2 { padding-inline: calc(0.9rem + 14px); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d3 { padding-inline: calc(0.9rem + 28px); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-d4 { padding-inline: calc(0.9rem + 42px); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-quote-line { font-style: italic; font-size: 1.1em; }
/* View's vertical rhythm, rebuilt from line boxes (live_preview_extension's
   docRhythmOf writes the px, from print's margins measured in this very
   sheet): two blocks a blank source line apart stand max(margin-bottom,
   margin-top) apart in print, their margins collapsed, so the blank line
   is exactly that tall (--fm-gap). A heading or a quote line carries no
   margin of its own (line decorations may never carry margins; the theme's
   own heading padding and rules reach the line through the host's
   retargeting, untouched). Without a blank line between two blocks (a
   paragraph straight under its heading) the collapsed gap stands above the
   second block's first line (--fm-gap-top, a block-level ::before). */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-blank { font-size: 0.65em; line-height: var(--fm-gap-end, var(--fm-gap, var(--fm-separator))); padding-bottom: var(--fm-stretch, 0px); }
/* --fm-gap-end: at a page's foot the blank line takes the room left for
   it (stretchField's ends), as print drops a margin past the foot. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-content { --fm-separator: var(--fm-p-margin, calc(0.65 * 1lh)); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-gap::before { content: ""; display: block; height: var(--fm-gap-top, 0px); }
/* --fm-stretch: the page layout's share of a page's leftover for this
   separator (live_preview_extension stretchField), so a page that ends
   because its next block moved reads as set rather than cut short. */
/* Further blank lines in a run are lines of space in the document (the
   renderer's .fm-space, one line tall). Margins do not collapse through a
   line of space: the run's first blank line is the previous block's whole
   bottom margin, and the last line of space carries the next block's whole
   top margin under it (--fm-gap-bottom). */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-space { font-size: 1em; padding-bottom: var(--fm-gap-bottom, 0px); }
/* Print's list items carry 0.25em margins that collapse to one between
   items (and through the list's ends into the gaps around it): the second
   item onward takes that as padding (a class from the source, never a
   sibling selector: CodeMirror stands a placeholder in for an unrendered
   neighbour), so a list stands the same height. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-li.cm-fm-li-next { padding-top: var(--fm-li-gap, 0.25em); }
/* View's document opens flush with its first block: leading blank lines are
   not content there, and the body first-child rule drops its top margin (a cover
   even pulls itself up). The editor's page must open the same way, or every
   report starts with a strip of bare page ground above its cover. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-lead { height: 0; font-size: 0; line-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-first { margin-top: 0 !important; }
/* Section numbers on the editor's own heading lines (the rendered document
   uses a CSS counter; a cm-line is not a real heading). */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-secnum { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
/* A peer's caret inside a rendered block — the same bar, dot and name flag
   yCollab draws in a paragraph (its .cm-ySelectionCaret), positioned by the
   presence plugin since the text layer cannot reach into a widget. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-peer-caret {
  position: absolute;
  width: 2px;
  margin-left: -1px;
  pointer-events: auto;
  z-index: 4;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-peer-caret::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: -2px;
  top: -3px;
  width: 6px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: inherit;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-peer-caret::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: -6px;
  right: -6px;
  top: -8px;
  bottom: 0;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-peer-caret__name {
  position: absolute;
  left: -1px;
  bottom: 100%;
  padding: 1px 4px;
  border-radius: 3px 3px 3px 0;
  font: 11px/1.3 system-ui, sans-serif;
  color: #fff;
  white-space: nowrap;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.2s ease-in-out;
  pointer-events: none;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-peer-caret:hover > .fm-peer-caret__name { opacity: 1; }
/* CodeMirror's find panel is app chrome sitting on a themed document sheet:
   give it the app's own surface rather than letting the report's typography
   reach it. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-panels {
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #111111;
  border-color: rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.15);
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
  font-size: 13px;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-panels input, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-panels button, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-panels label {
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 12px;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-panels .cm-textfield {
  border: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.2);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 2px 6px;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-panels .cm-button {
  border-radius: 4px;
  background-image: none;
  background: rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.06);
  border: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.12);
}
/* Two classes: the general first-child clamp below is a later rule of equal
   weight, and would otherwise win the tie. The first block of the document
   has no top margin in print either (the paged sheet's title rule). */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region.fm-live-region--first > .fm-peer-layer + :not(.fm-page-gutter, .fm-page-split),
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region.fm-live-region--first > .fm-page-gutter--inner + :not(.fm-page-split),
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region.fm-live-region--first > .fm-page-split + * { margin-top: 0 !important; }
/* Widgets render REAL html inside .cm-content, which is white-space:pre-wrap
   (CodeMirror needs it for the text). Inherited into a widget, every newline
   the renderer emits between tags becomes a phantom line box — two extra
   lines in every callout, one after every grid. Rendered content collapses
   whitespace exactly like the preview does. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-chrome { white-space: normal; }
/* CodeMirror's line wrapping (overflow-wrap: anywhere, word-break:
   break-word) inherited into a widget makes every character a break
   opportunity, and a table's columns then shrink to single letters.
   Rendered content wraps at words, as print does. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-chrome { overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: normal; }
/* The editor's own lines wrap as print's paragraphs do: pre-wrap lets a
   space at a line's end hang, where break-spaces (CodeMirror's choice for
   its line wrapping) gives it room and wraps the word before it a line
   early, one line taller than print for the same paragraph. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-content.cm-lineWrapping { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: normal; }
/* A quote's lines carry the box's own padding (print's 0.2em, measured as
   --fm-bq-pad) on the run's first and last line and nothing between; the
   quote's margins are the blank lines' beside it (the rhythm). The classes
   come from the source, never from a sibling selector. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-bq { padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-bq.cm-fm-bq-first { padding-top: var(--fm-bq-pad, 0.2em); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-bq.cm-fm-bq-last { padding-bottom: var(--fm-bq-pad, 0.2em); }
/* A heading line carries no margin of its own: the blank line above it is
   the whole collapsed gap (the rhythm), and the theme's own heading padding
   and rules (an h2's 0.25em under-rule) reach the line through the host's
   retargeting. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-li { --fm-li-depth: 1; position: relative; padding-left: calc(var(--fm-li-indent, 1.4em) * var(--fm-li-depth)); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-li.cm-fm-li-d2 { --fm-li-depth: 2; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-li.cm-fm-li-d3 { --fm-li-depth: 3; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-li.cm-fm-li-d4 { --fm-li-depth: 4; }
/* A plain markdown blockquote takes the theme's own blockquote treatment —
   the host retargets those rules onto this class, margins neutralised. */
/* A concealed role mark's label can sit inside what Lezer tokenized as a
   shortcut-reference link; the highlight style's underline is noise there. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-mark { text-decoration: none !important; }
/* …except an explicit underline mark, which must survive that strip (and
   the heading strip the host adds) at the same strength. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-mark.fm-mark--u { text-decoration: underline !important; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-mark.fm-mark--hl { padding: 0.05em 0.2em; border-radius: min(var(--fm-radius), 3px); }
/* Syntax hidden inside an ACTIVE text island (the leading heading marker,
   role-mark wrappers): display:none keeps it out of the visual flow while
   textContent still carries it, so a commit round-trips byte-identically. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-island-syntax { display: none; }
/* The box layer carries a NEGATIVE z-index (CodeMirror's below-text layers
   all do). A negative-z child only paints above its ancestor's background
   when that ancestor is a stacking context — isolate the scroller so the
   boxes can never fall behind the page ground. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-scroller { isolation: isolate; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-box {
  position: absolute;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  pointer-events: none;
  /* The structural classes carry flow margins; an absolutely positioned box
     must not let them shift it off its measured rectangle. Important, because
     the retargeted theme rules land later in the sheet. */
  margin: 0 !important;
}
/* A collapsed widget's render carries the preview's own block margins
   (--fm-mt/--fm-mb, declared by each block's rule in the structure sheet).
   In the editor the blank source line beside the block IS the gap (the
   rhythm rules above), so the widget keeps none of them: its first CONTENT
   child (the child after the peer layer, or after the page seam and the
   "continues" flag that stand before it when the block opens a page or
   runs past one) takes only --fm-gap-top, the collapsed gap of a block with
   no blank line above it, and its last child no margin at all. The box is
   the same wherever the block stands, seam or no seam: the page layout
   takes every block's box from the height map, and a seam that changed the
   box would make the layout that placed it find another height and move it
   away, then back, every frame (the flicker of 2026-09-10). Print keeps a
   block's whole top margin at the top of a page: the SEAM carries it there
   as its padding-bottom (pageBoxPlugin writes it), so the page reads as
   print's and the block's box does not change. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > .fm-peer-layer + :not(.fm-page-gutter, .fm-page-split),
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > .fm-page-gutter--inner + :not(.fm-page-split),
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > .fm-page-split + * { margin-top: var(--fm-gap-top, 0px) !important; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > *:last-child { margin-bottom: 0 !important; }
/* A leaf rendered by its own widget (contents, a page break marker) is one
   block too: the same clamp. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-leaf > :first-child { margin-top: var(--fm-gap-top, 0px) !important; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-leaf > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0 !important; }
/* A fenced code block as print's pre: the fence lines are the pre's 0.9em
   padding rows (their text a small label), the code lines its rows at the
   body's line height with the code in an inline span at print's 0.9em
   monospace (pre > code), unwrapped as print's overflow-x: auto leaves
   them. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-code-fence {
  font-size: 0.7em; line-height: calc(0.9em / 0.7); color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt); padding-left: calc(1.1em / 0.7); padding-right: calc(1.1em / 0.7);
  white-space: pre; overflow: hidden;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-code-open { border-radius: var(--fm-radius) var(--fm-radius) 0 0; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-code-close { border-radius: 0 0 var(--fm-radius) var(--fm-radius); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-code-line {
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt); padding-left: 1.1em; padding-right: 1.1em;
  white-space: pre; overflow: hidden;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-codetext { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; }
/* A thematic break is print's hr: its margins are the blank lines' beside
   it (the rhythm); the widget's box is the rule alone, with a click target
   around it that takes no room (negative margins against its padding). */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-hr { padding: 12px 0; margin: -12px 0; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-hr > hr { margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }
/* The contents block's entries carry their page numbers in the editor as
   in print (pageBoxPlugin writes data-fm-page from the page layout, where
   print uses target-counter), laid out the same way. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-leaf .fm-toc__item a { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 1em; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-leaf .fm-toc__item a[data-fm-page]::after {
  content: attr(data-fm-page); color: var(--fm-ink-muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
/* A cover that fills its page ends it: the sheet is its box, and its
   bottom margin would stand the page box that much over the sheet. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > .fm-cover.fm-cover--fill { margin-top: 0 !important; margin-bottom: 0 !important; }
/* The blank source line after a filling cover has no page to stand on
   (the cover is the whole sheet): a line of no height. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region:has(> .fm-cover.fm-cover--fill) + .cm-line.cm-fm-blank { height: 0; padding: 0 !important; line-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
/* The page break marker takes no room, as in print: the labelled rule is
   laid over the foot of the page it ends. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-leaf.cm-fm-leaf--marker { position: relative; height: 0; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-leaf--marker > .fm-pagebreak.fm-pagebreak--editor { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; margin: 0 !important; }
/* The seam and the flag inside a widget are chrome, not the block: no
   margin of their own. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > .fm-page-gutter--inner, :root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region > .fm-page-split { margin-top: 0 !important; }
/* The peer layer (carets, presence) sits first in every widget and covers
   it; it is not content, so the clamp above addresses the child after it. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-peer-layer {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 4;
}
/* GAP above the box is page-side; the extra 8px is interior headroom so the
   title clears the box's own top border (the box starts at +GAP exactly). */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-chrome-open { padding-top: 24px; padding-bottom: 0.2rem; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-chrome-cap {
  height: 10px;
  padding-bottom: 16px;
  box-sizing: content-box;
}
/* Chrome widgets replace the fence lines entirely: the block's real header
   (title bar, kicker) on the block's own ground, and a thin end cap. The
   syntax never shows in Edit mode — attrs are toolbar territory. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-chrome { cursor: pointer; }
/* An in-place text editor keeps its element's rendered box; the dotted
   underline marks the editable surface, as on the labels. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-text-edit { cursor: text; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-text-edit:hover { text-decoration: underline dotted; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-text-edit:focus { outline: 1px dashed var(--fm-accent-text); outline-offset: 2px; text-decoration: none; }
/* No ring on the active region: blocks look exactly as View renders them even
   with the caret inside (the class still drives ghost placeholders). */
/* Click-to-edit labels in chrome: a text cursor and a quiet dotted underline
   on hover say "this is editable"; an empty label shows its placeholder so a
   cleared title can always be brought back. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-attr { cursor: text; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-attr:hover { text-decoration: underline dotted; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-attr:focus {
  outline: none;
  text-decoration: underline dotted;
  text-underline-offset: 3px;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-attr:empty::before {
  content: attr(data-placeholder);
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  font-style: italic;
}
/* ── Page boxes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The paginator says where each printed page starts; the editor draws the
   seam there: the ending page's running footer, then a strip of app chrome
   running edge to edge of the sheet (the bleed vars), then the next page
   begins. Inside a rendered block the same element is injected before the
   child that starts the page; between plain lines it is a block widget. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter {
  display: block;
  /* No block margins: the seam's padding-top is the page filler, measured
     exactly (pageBoxPlugin), so nothing else may add to the page's height. */
  margin: 0 var(--fm-bleed-margin);
  padding: 0;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  text-transform: none;
  letter-spacing: 0;
  white-space: normal;
  pointer-events: none;
  user-select: none;
}
/* The printed page's bottom margin (--fm-page-margin: 18mm at the sheet's
   scale, set by the host), with the running footer sitting in it as the
   PDF's margin box does. A page's content area is the sheet less its top
   and bottom margins, exactly as in print, so the editor and the paginator
   agree on what fits on a page. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter__foot {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 1em;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  height: var(--fm-page-margin, 77px);
  padding: 0 var(--fm-bleed-pad);
  /* Print's margin boxes: 8.5pt in the body face at the document's own
     line height (inherited, as the margin box inherits it), centred in
     the margin (report_fastr_paged.ts). */
  font-size: 8.5pt;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
/* The gap between two sheets: the app's own ground, the same colour as the
   pane either side of it, so it reads as the pane showing between two sheets
   (in dark mode too). The sheets' cut edges are the same hairline as their
   side edges (the scroller's), in the app's border colour; no shadow, which
   tinted the gap darker than the pane beside it. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter__band {
  display: block;
  height: 30px;
  background: var(--forge-surface-2, #f2f2f2);
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 1px 0 var(--forge-surface-3, #d9d9d9),
    inset 0 -1px 0 var(--forge-surface-3, #d9d9d9);
}
/* The next page's top margin. Before the document's first line too, when
   page 1 is not a cover (a cover has no margins). */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter__head {
  display: block;
  height: var(--fm-page-margin, 77px);
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-head { display: block; }
/* A seam INSIDE a rendered block (a callout, band or steps block that
   continues on the next page, or one that opens a page): centred on the
   block's content box, which sits centred on the sheet, and as wide as the
   sheet, painted with the DOCUMENT's ground (--fm-page-ground, the tone or
   colour the :::report line sets, put on the scroller by the editor's
   ground plugin; the theme's page colour when there is none) so the
   block's box visibly stops above it and resumes below, as print draws
   it. It must not read as one of the block's children: no padding, border,
   counter or generated number. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter--inner:not(.fm-page-gutter--cell), :root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter--cell .fm-page-gutter__sheet {
  position: relative;
  left: 50%;
  width: var(--fm-sheet, 794px);
  /* The estimate; pageBoxPlugin measures the strip against the sheet and
     writes the exact margin and width inline (a block's own left border
     puts its content box off centre). */
  margin: 0 0 0 calc(-0.5 * var(--fm-sheet, 794px));
}
/* Inside a table the seam is a row of its own (seamRow): the cell carries
   the padding and the ground, its strip reaches the sheet from a box with
   no intrinsic inline size, so the table's columns are not widened. */
:root .fm-live-scope tr.fm-page-gutter-row { border: 0 !important; background: none !important; }
/* A table's header rows repeated after an in-table seam (the host retargets
   the theme's thead th rules onto them): inert copies. */
:root .fm-live-scope tr.fm-page-gutter-repeat { pointer-events: none; user-select: none; }
:root .fm-live-scope td.fm-page-gutter--cell {
  /* A cell, whatever the seam's own display; no margins on a cell. It is
     only as wide as the table, so it takes no sheet edges: the scroller's
     show beside the table. */
  box-shadow: none !important;
  display: table-cell;
  margin: 0;
  padding-top: 0;
  padding-bottom: 0;
  vertical-align: top;
  height: auto;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter--cell > .fm-page-gutter__contain { contain: inline-size; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter--inner {
  padding-left: 0 !important;
  padding-right: 0 !important;
  border: 0 !important;
  border-radius: 0 !important;
  /* The block's own shadow never, but the SHEET's side edges (the scroller's
     inset hairlines, which this strip paints over). */
  box-shadow: inset 1px 0 0 var(--forge-surface-3, #d9d9d9),
    inset -1px 0 0 var(--forge-surface-3, #d9d9d9) !important;
  background: var(--fm-page-ground, var(--fm-page));
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  counter-increment: none !important;
  z-index: 1;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter--inner::before, :root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-gutter--inner::after { content: none !important; }
/* A seam INSIDE a wrapped line, before the row that opens the page (a
   paragraph running on: PageRowSeamWidget). A float whose margin box is as
   wide as the line box never fits beside text, so it is set down between
   two rows and the paragraph wraps exactly as it would without it. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line > .fm-page-gutter.fm-page-gutter--row {
  float: left;
  clear: both;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: calc(100% + 2 * var(--fm-bleed-pad));
  margin: 0 var(--fm-bleed-margin);
  text-indent: 0;
  line-height: var(--fm-body-leading, 1.55);
}
/* Between plain lines the gutter is a block widget: no line box of its own,
   the same seam geometry as inside a block. After the last line, the last
   page's foot and filler. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-gutter, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-fm-page-end { display: block; }
/* A :::pagebreak line: invisible on the page, a labelled rule in the editor
   so the author can see where they forced a break (and delete it). */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-pagebreak.fm-pagebreak--editor {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.8em;
  height: auto;
  margin: 0.6em 0;
  overflow: visible;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  font-size: 0.7em;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  cursor: pointer;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-pagebreak.fm-pagebreak--editor::before, :root .fm-live-scope .fm-pagebreak.fm-pagebreak--editor::after {
  content: "";
  flex: 1;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--fm-ink-muted);
}
/* A logos row with nothing in it yet: a dashed slot the author clicks to
   choose the logos (the widget adds the label). Border-box, so the slot is
   print's box to the pixel. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-logos--empty {
  justify-content: center;
  border: 1px dashed var(--fm-ink-muted);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  box-sizing: border-box;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  cursor: pointer;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-logos__empty { font-size: 0.8em; }
/* A block the paginator had to split because it is taller than a page: a
   chip laid over the block's top corner, out of the flow, so the block's
   box is print's box and the layout that placed the seam is not moved by
   its own flag. */
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-live-region--split { position: relative; }
:root .fm-live-scope .fm-page-split {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0.4em;
  right: 0.4em;
  z-index: 3;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.15em 0.6em;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--fm-warning, #b45309);
  color: #ffffff;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  font-size: 0.68em;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  text-transform: none;
  pointer-events: none;
  user-select: none;
}
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-line.cm-fm-split { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--fm-warning, #b45309); }
/* The document is the ground; the code-editor affordances step back. */
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-cursor, :root .fm-live-scope .cm-dropCursor { border-left-color: var(--fm-ink); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-activeLine { background: transparent; }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-content ::selection { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent) 25%, transparent); }
:root .fm-live-scope .cm-selectionBackground { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent) 25%, transparent) !important; }

css/default:
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap');
:root {
  --fm-page: #ffffff;
  --fm-paper: #ffffff;
  --fm-warm: #936653;
  --fm-light-ink: #fcfcfb;
  --fm-dark-ink: #24292e;
  --fm-surface: #f3f4f3;
  --fm-surface-alt: #ebebeb;
  --fm-ink: #24292e;
  --fm-ink-muted: #76797c;
  --fm-accent: #4e6f94;
  --fm-border: #d5d6d6;
  --fm-radius: 6px;
  --fm-border-width: 1px;
  /* What a border at the theme's width takes beyond the default theme's
     1px: every structure rule drawn at --fm-border-width gives it back out
     of the padding beside it, so a heavier theme's boxes stand as tall and
     hold as wide a column as the default theme's (FASTR_THEME_SPECS). */
  --fm-border-give: calc(1px - 1px);
  --fm-body-tracking: 0em;
  --fm-body-size: 16px;
  --fm-body-leading: 1.55;
  --fm-bullet: "\2022 ";
  --fm-fit-caption: 1;
  --fm-fit-callout-title: 1;
  --fm-fit-card-title: 1;
  --fm-fit-stat-value: 1;
  --fm-fit-stat-label: 1;
  --fm-fit-kicker: 1;
  --fm-fit-th: 1;
  --fm-fit-quote: 1;
  --fm-fit-cite: 1;
  --fm-font-body: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --fm-font-heading: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --fm-heading-weight: 700;
  --fm-heading-tracking: -0.01em;
  --fm-heading-case: none;
  --fm-measure: 56rem;
  --fm-callout-color: #4e6f94;
  --fm-h1-size: 2.15em;
  --fm-h1-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  --fm-h1-line-height: 1.2;
  --fm-h1-fit: 1;
  --fm-h2-size: 1.55em;
  --fm-h2-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  --fm-h2-line-height: 1.2;
  --fm-h2-fit: 1;
  --fm-h3-size: 1.2em;
  --fm-h3-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  --fm-h3-line-height: 1.2;
  --fm-h3-fit: 1;
  --fm-h4-size: 1em;
  --fm-h4-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  --fm-h4-line-height: 1.2;
  --fm-h4-fit: 1;
  --fm-h5-size: 1em;
  --fm-h5-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  --fm-h5-line-height: 1.2;
  --fm-h5-fit: 1;
  --fm-h6-size: 1em;
  --fm-h6-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  --fm-h6-line-height: 1.2;
  --fm-h6-fit: 1;
  --fm-paper-ground: #ebebeb;
  --fm-paper-ground-ink: #24292e;
  --fm-ink-ground: #24292e;
  --fm-ink-ground-ink: #fcfcfb;
  --fm-accent-ground: #4e6f94;
  --fm-accent-ground-ink: #fcfcfb;
  --fm-warm-ground: #936653;
  --fm-warm-ground-ink: #fcfcfb;
  --fm-accent-text: #4e6f94;
  --fm-mark-accent-weight: inherit;
  --fm-info-light: #4e6f94;
  --fm-info-dark: #9caec2;
  --fm-success-light: #4e6f94;
  --fm-success-dark: #9caec2;
  --fm-warning-light: #988858;
  --fm-warning-dark: #c5bca1;
  --fm-danger-light: #936653;
  --fm-danger-dark: #c2aa9f;
  --fm-info: var(--fm-info-light);
  --fm-success: var(--fm-success-light);
  --fm-warning: var(--fm-warning-light);
  --fm-danger: var(--fm-danger-light);
}

html, body {
  background: var(--fm-page);
  color: var(--fm-ink);
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-body-tracking, 0em);
  /* Full-bleed geometry, defined ONCE: a band cancels the centred column with
     a viewport-width negative margin, then insets its own content back to the
     measure. Print and the scoped picker tiles have no viewport to bleed into,
     so they neutralise the pair here rather than resetting each selector. */
  --fm-bleed-margin: calc(50% - 50vw);
  --fm-bleed-pad: max(1.5rem, calc((100vw - var(--fm-measure)) / 2 + 1.5rem));
}
/* The PAGE ground lives on <html>, not <body>: a full-bleed band is a body
   child that escapes the column with a viewport-width negative margin, and
   document-level settings (:::report) are applied to <html> so they cover the
   whole page rather than just the text column. overflow-x on the root absorbs
   the scrollbar width that 100vw would otherwise overflow by. */
body { max-width: var(--fm-measure); background: transparent; }
/* The theme's body type (fastrBodyType). On <body>, never <html>: a rem
   is the root's, and the column and cover lengths are written in rem. A
   scoped sheet sets nothing here: the editor's lines read the same two
   vars on .cm-content (livePreviewTheme), and a picker tile sets its own. */
body { font-size: var(--fm-body-size); line-height: var(--fm-body-leading); }
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  color: var(--fm-ink);
  margin: calc(1.8em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)) 0 calc(0.4em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
}
/* An h1 is a SECTION (the cover carries the title): its own larger em
   gives it a little more room above than an h2 (FASTR_HEADING_SPACE). The
   document's first block has none (below, and the paged sheet's title
   rule); a cover's title sits where its layout puts it. --fm-h-fit is the
   level's width fit (FastrThemeSpec.headingFit): the size var is already
   divided by it, so every em a heading rule writes for its box (a margin, a
   rule's padding, a template's own size) multiplies by it to keep the
   default theme's box. */
h1 { --fm-h-fit: var(--fm-h1-fit, 1); font-size: var(--fm-h1-size); font-weight: var(--fm-h1-weight); line-height: var(--fm-h1-line-height); }
h2 { --fm-h-fit: var(--fm-h2-fit, 1); font-size: var(--fm-h2-size); font-weight: var(--fm-h2-weight); line-height: var(--fm-h2-line-height); }
h3 { --fm-h-fit: var(--fm-h3-fit, 1); font-size: var(--fm-h3-size); font-weight: var(--fm-h3-weight); line-height: var(--fm-h3-line-height); }
h4 { --fm-h-fit: var(--fm-h4-fit, 1); font-size: var(--fm-h4-size); font-weight: var(--fm-h4-weight); line-height: var(--fm-h4-line-height); }
h5 { --fm-h-fit: var(--fm-h5-fit, 1); font-size: var(--fm-h5-size); font-weight: var(--fm-h5-weight); line-height: var(--fm-h5-line-height); }
h6 { --fm-h-fit: var(--fm-h6-fit, 1); font-size: var(--fm-h6-size); font-weight: var(--fm-h6-weight); line-height: var(--fm-h6-line-height); }
h1 { margin-top: calc(1.5em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
/* The default theme's h2 rule, as every theme's box: a theme recolours it,
   restyles it, or draws a heavier one by giving the extra width back out of
   the padding (the geometry rule at FASTR_THEME_SPECS). */
h2 {
  padding-bottom: calc(0.25em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
}
body > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
p { margin: 0 0 1em; }
/* A paragraph's or heading's own alignment ({align=…},
   fastr_paragraph_align.ts); a class beats a theme's own heading rule. */
.fm-align-left { text-align: left; }
.fm-align-center { text-align: center; }
.fm-align-right { text-align: right; }
.fm-align-justify { text-align: justify; }
/* A blank source line beyond the paragraph separator (report_fastr_markdown's
   fm_spaces): one line of the body's height, empty, exactly the height the
   editor gives that line, so Enter moves the page the same way on both. */
.fm-space { height: 1lh; margin: 0; }
a { color: var(--fm-accent); }
strong { font-weight: 700; }
ul, ol { margin: 0 0 1em; --fm-mt: 0px; --fm-mb: 1em; padding-left: 1.4em; list-style: none; }
li { margin: 0.25em 0; position: relative; }
/* The markers as glyphs at the left of the list's own indent, as the editor
   draws them on its lines (cm-fm-bullet), so an item's text starts where the
   editor's does. The contents block is an ol of its own. */
ul > li::before { content: var(--fm-bullet, "\2022"); position: absolute; left: -1.4em; width: 1.4em; }
ol:not(.fm-toc__list) { counter-reset: fm-ol; }
ol:not(.fm-toc__list) > li { counter-increment: fm-ol; }
ol:not(.fm-toc__list) > li::before { content: counter(fm-ol) "."; position: absolute; left: -1.4em; width: 1.4em; }
hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--fm-border); margin: 2em 0; }
code {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size: 0.9em;
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt);
  padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
  border-radius: min(var(--fm-radius), 3px);
}
/* The browser's own 1em margins, declared: the editor measures print's
   margins under the app's base sheet, which zeroes a pre's. */
pre {
  margin: 1em 0;
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: 0.9em 1.1em;
  overflow-x: auto;
}
pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }
table { width: 100%; margin: 0 0 1.4em; --fm-mt: 0px; --fm-mb: 1.4em; font-size: 0.94em; }
th, td {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fm-border);
  padding: 0.5em 0.7em;
  text-align: left;
  vertical-align: top;
}
/* tr.fm-page-gutter-repeat is the editor's copy of a table's header rows on
   a page the table continues on, which print's runner clones into a real
   thead (live_preview_extension): it takes the header treatment too, or the
   continuation stands a pixel short of print's. */
thead th, tr.fm-page-gutter-repeat > th {
  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--fm-ink);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: calc(1em / var(--fm-fit-th, 1));
  line-height: calc(var(--fm-body-leading, 1.55) * var(--fm-fit-th, 1));
  padding: calc(0.5em * var(--fm-fit-th, 1)) calc(0.7em * var(--fm-fit-th, 1));
}
blockquote {
  margin: 1.4em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.4em;
  --fm-mb: 1.4em;
  padding: 0.2em 0 0.2em 1.1em;
  border-left: 3px solid var(--fm-border);
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
}
/* The quote's own padding sets it off; its paragraphs bring no margin of
   their own to the box (the editor draws the quote as lines and has none). */
blockquote > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
blockquote > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
/* A word longer than the column (a URL) breaks rather than run past the
   page; the editor's lines wrap the same way. */
p, li, td, th, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 { overflow-wrap: break-word; }

/* ── Figures (an embed on its own line becomes a captioned figure) ────────── */
.fm-figure { margin: 1.6em 0; --fm-mt: 1.6em; --fm-mb: 1.6em; }
/* A figure is the width its author gave it, the same wherever it falls
   (fastr_markdown_blocks.ts, "Figure widths"): the text column by default,
   a share of it at width=small|medium (--fm-fig-share). Its height is its
   own aspect at that width. The ONLY height limit is the page ceiling
   (FIGURE_CAP: --fm-page-area, which the paged sheet and the editor's page
   boxes set, less the measured figure reserve, so a section heading and the
   figure always share a page; a browser window falls back to its own
   height), which only a figure shaped taller than the page ever meets; it
   then narrows, centred, to the tallest that fits. An image is never
   stretched past its own pixels (width: auto). */
.fm-figure--small { --fm-fig-share: 0.5; }
.fm-figure--medium { --fm-fig-share: 0.75; }
.fm-figure img {
  display: block;
  width: auto;
  max-width: calc(100% * var(--fm-fig-share, 1));
  max-height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) - var(--fm-fig-reserve, calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) * 0.15)));
  margin-inline: auto;
}
/* The editor's stand-in while a figure renders (report_html.ts): the same
   width and ceiling, so the page flow does not move when the raster
   replaces it. */
.fm-figure .report-embed-pending {
  width: calc(100% * var(--fm-fig-share, 1));
  max-height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) - var(--fm-fig-reserve, calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) * 0.15)));
  margin-inline: auto;
}
/* The editor's LIVE chart mount (live_preview_extension applyFigureSize):
   the raster's aspect (--fm-fig-w/h) at the figure's share of the column,
   under the same ceiling, narrowed and centred exactly as the img above,
   sized before the chart draws; the canvas inside is cut to the box (it lays
   out to the same aspect, give or take a pixel of rounding). */
.fm-figure [data-embed-kind="figure"][data-fm-sized] {
  --fm-fig-cap: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) - var(--fm-fig-reserve, calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) * 0.15)));
  aspect-ratio: var(--fm-fig-w) / var(--fm-fig-h);
  width: min(calc(100% * var(--fm-fig-share, 1)), calc(var(--fm-fig-cap) * var(--fm-fig-w) / var(--fm-fig-h)));
  margin-inline: auto;
  overflow: hidden;
}
/* A mount still waiting for its size draws its chart at the chart's own
   height meanwhile: under the ceiling like a printed figure, so a figure can
   never stand a page tall while it waits (the editor sizes the mount from
   the drawn canvas itself a frame later). */
.fm-figure [data-embed-kind="figure"][data-fm-pending] {
  max-height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) - var(--fm-fig-reserve, calc(var(--fm-page-area, 100vh) * 0.15)));
  overflow: hidden;
}
/* A restyled text role (a caption, a callout's title, a stat's value…) is
   set at its size divided by the theme's width fit for it (--fm-fit-<role>,
   FastrThemeSpec.textFit) on leading multiplied by it, and every em its box
   writes multiplies by it: the role wraps where the default theme's does and
   stands as tall, whatever face, case or tracking the theme gives it. */
.fm-figure__caption {
  margin-top: calc(0.5em * var(--fm-fit-caption, 1));
  font-size: calc(0.85em / var(--fm-fit-caption, 1));
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  line-height: calc(1.4 * var(--fm-fit-caption, 1));
}

/* ── Callouts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-callout {
  margin: 1.5em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.5em;
  --fm-mb: 1.5em;
  padding: 1em 1.2em;
  background: var(--fm-surface);
  border-left: 4px solid var(--fm-callout-color);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
}
.fm-callout > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fm-callout__title {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: calc(1em / var(--fm-fit-callout-title, 1));
  line-height: calc(var(--fm-body-leading, 1.55) * var(--fm-fit-callout-title, 1));
  color: var(--fm-callout-color);
  margin-bottom: calc(0.35em * var(--fm-fit-callout-title, 1));
}
.fm-callout--note { --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-callout--info { --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-info); }
.fm-callout--success { --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-success); }
.fm-callout--warning { --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-warning); }
.fm-callout--danger { --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-danger); }

/* ── Inline role marks — [fell 12 points]{.danger} ────────────────────────── */
/* The token is read HERE, on the span, never through a --fm-mark-* alias: a
   --fm-mark-danger: var(--fm-danger) declared on :root would substitute at
   computed-value time and inherit the SUBSTITUTED colour, so re-scoping
   --fm-danger inside a dark band would not move the mark. Reading it on the
   span means every ground rule that re-scopes the semantic tokens already
   works for marks, with no rule of its own. Doubled class for the same reason
   the tones double theirs — a theme's extraCss must not outrank a role. */
/* An accent mark must never be a no-op. In a theme whose accent cannot carry
   text on the page (Brutalist's yellow) or IS the ink (Minimal),
   --fm-accent-text degrades to ink by design — so those themes, and only
   those, mark the phrase with weight instead. */
.fm-mark.fm-mark--accent {
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
  font-weight: var(--fm-mark-accent-weight, inherit);
}
.fm-mark.fm-mark--hl { padding: 0.05em 0.2em; border-radius: min(var(--fm-radius), 3px); }
.fm-mark.fm-mark--muted { color: var(--fm-ink-muted); }
.fm-mark.fm-mark--danger { color: var(--fm-danger); }
.fm-mark.fm-mark--warning { color: var(--fm-warning); }
.fm-mark.fm-mark--success { color: var(--fm-success); }
.fm-mark.fm-mark--info { color: var(--fm-info); }
.fm-tone--accent .fm-mark--danger,
.fm-tone--accent .fm-mark--warning,
.fm-tone--accent .fm-mark--success,
.fm-tone--accent .fm-mark--info,
.fm-tone--warm .fm-mark--danger,
.fm-tone--warm .fm-mark--warning,
.fm-tone--warm .fm-mark--success,
.fm-tone--warm .fm-mark--info { color: var(--fm-ink); }

/* ── Tiles & cards ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-tiles {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1em;
  margin: 1.6em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.6em;
  --fm-mb: 1.6em;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
}
.fm-tiles--1 { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
.fm-tiles--2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
.fm-tiles--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
.fm-tiles--4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
/* A grid has no padding, so a tone on the ROW would show only through the gaps.
   Give it room and the ground reads as a panel holding the tiles. */
.fm-tiles.fm-tone, .fm-tiles.fm-has-bg,
.fm-columns.fm-tone, .fm-columns.fm-has-bg {
  padding: 1.2em;
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
}
.fm-card {
  /* A card on its own in the flow keeps its distance like a callout; in a
     tiles grid the gap is the grid's. The editor shows a card as a widget
     with a blank line and 0.2em of box gap on each side, which is this. */
  margin: 1.2em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.2em;
  --fm-mb: 1.2em;
  background: var(--fm-surface);
  border: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: calc(1em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px)) calc(1.1em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
}
.fm-tiles > .fm-card { margin: 0; }
.fm-card > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fm-card__title {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: calc(0.95em / var(--fm-fit-card-title, 1));
  line-height: calc(var(--fm-body-leading, 1.55) * var(--fm-fit-card-title, 1));
  margin-bottom: calc(0.4em * var(--fm-fit-card-title, 1));
}

/* ── Stats ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-stat {
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt);
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: 1em 1.1em;
  margin: 1.2em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.2em;
  --fm-mb: 1.2em;
}
.fm-tiles .fm-stat, .fm-columns .fm-stat { margin: 0; }
.fm-stat > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fm-stat__value {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: calc(2.1em / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1));
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  line-height: calc(1.05 * var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1));
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
.fm-stat__label {
  font-size: calc(0.85em / var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
  line-height: calc(var(--fm-body-leading, 1.55) * var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  margin-top: calc(0.25em * var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
}
/* Top-aligned: on the baseline, the line box around the pill took the body
   face's ascent and descent, and a stat stood a fraction of a pixel taller
   on one theme than another. */
.fm-stat__delta {
  display: inline-block;
  vertical-align: top;
  margin-top: 0.5em;
  font-size: 0.8em;
  font-weight: 700;
  padding: 0.1em 0.45em;
  border-radius: calc(var(--fm-radius) * 999);
}
.fm-stat__delta--up {
  color: var(--fm-success);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-success) 16%, transparent);
}
.fm-stat__delta--down {
  color: var(--fm-danger);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-danger) 16%, transparent);
}
.fm-stat__delta--flat {
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-ink) 8%, transparent);
}

/* ── Columns ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-columns {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1.5em;
  margin: 1.6em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.6em;
  --fm-mb: 1.6em;
  align-items: start;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
}
.fm-columns--1 { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
.fm-columns--2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
.fm-columns--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
.fm-columns--4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
.fm-col > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
/* A column's first block (its heading, mostly) never carries its own top
   margin: the row has one, and a heading's would drop the column's text
   below its neighbour's the moment one column is coloured and the other not. */
.fm-col > :first-child, .fm-col > .cm-fm-col-ghost + * { margin-top: 0; }
/* A row with ANY coloured column is a set of panels: every column takes the
   panel inset, coloured or not, so the text of the two sides stays aligned
   and colouring one column never reflows the others'
   (fm-columns--panels, set by the renderer). */
.fm-columns--panels > .fm-col {
  padding: 1em 1.2em;
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  align-self: stretch;
}
/* A toned or painted column is a panel: text flush with a coloured edge reads
   as a mistake, so it takes the same inset a toned grid does, and its first
   block sits at the top of the panel rather than under its own margin.
   Panels in one row are also read as a SET (the two sides of a comparison,
   which is what the brief asks a toned columns pair to be), so each takes
   the row's full height however its text wraps: two panels an inch apart
   read as a mistake where two columns of plain text simply end where they
   end, which is why the row itself still aligns to the start. */
.fm-col.fm-tone, .fm-col.fm-has-bg {
  padding: 1em 1.2em;
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  align-self: stretch;
}
.fm-col.fm-tone > :first-child, .fm-col.fm-has-bg > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
.fm-col--span2 { grid-column: span 2; }
.fm-col--span3 { grid-column: span 3; }
.fm-col--span4 { grid-column: span 4; }

/* ── Pull quote ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-quote {
  margin: 1.8em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.8em;
  --fm-mb: 1.8em;
  padding: 0.2em 0 0.2em 1.2em;
  border-left: 4px solid var(--fm-accent);
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: 1.1em;
  line-height: 1.45;
  color: var(--fm-ink);
}
/* The quote's fit is its words' (its box keeps its own em, which the
   editor reads its margins in). */
.fm-quote > p {
  font-size: calc(1em / var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
  line-height: calc(1.45 * var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
  margin-bottom: calc(1em * var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
}
.fm-quote > p:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fm-quote__cite {
  display: block;
  margin-top: calc(0.6em * var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  font-size: calc(0.72em / var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  line-height: calc(1.45 * var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  font-style: normal;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
}

/* Unknown block name — still groups its content rather than swallowing it. */
.fm-block { margin: 1.2em 0; }

/* ── Tones: grounds by ROLE ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* A tone re-scopes the ink TOKENS rather than setting color directly, so every
   descendant that reads --fm-ink (headings, muted labels, borders, rules)
   follows the ground automatically. That is also why a dark band re-inks its
   charts: the raster ground probe reads the computed background behind the
   figure, which these rules paint. */
/* The colour must be re-declared here, not just the token: an element inherits
   its parent's COMPUTED colour, which was resolved against the root ink before
   this block re-scoped --fm-ink. Headings re-resolve it (they set colour
   explicitly); paragraphs would otherwise stay dark on a dark band. */
/* Doubled for specificity, like the variants below: this rule re-declares the
   COLOUR (a child inherits its parent's computed colour, so re-scoping the ink
   token alone is not enough) and must outrank a theme's own element rules. */
.fm-tone.fm-tone { background: var(--fm-paper-ground); color: var(--fm-ink); }
/* The tone rules themselves are per theme: buildFastrToneCss. */
/* A theme may paint a heading WITH the accent (a highlighter mark). On a ground
   that is already a hue, that renders the heading invisible or garish, so the
   two hue grounds clear it. Discovered as a blank yellow cover. */
.fm-tone--accent h1, .fm-tone--accent h2, .fm-tone--accent h3,
.fm-tone--warm h1, .fm-tone--warm h2, .fm-tone--warm h3 {
  background: none;
  padding-inline: 0;
}

/* ── Literal ink (a bg colour's luminance decides it when not given) ──────── */
.fm-ink--light {
  --fm-ink: var(--fm-light-ink);
  --fm-accent: var(--fm-light-ink);
  --fm-accent-text: var(--fm-light-ink);
  --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-light-ink);
  --fm-ink-muted: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-light-ink) 72%, transparent);
  --fm-border: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-light-ink) 26%, transparent);
  --fm-surface: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-light-ink) 10%, transparent);
  --fm-surface-alt: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-light-ink) 16%, transparent);
  color: var(--fm-light-ink);
  --fm-info: var(--fm-info-dark);
  --fm-success: var(--fm-success-dark);
  --fm-warning: var(--fm-warning-dark);
  --fm-danger: var(--fm-danger-dark);
}
.fm-ink--dark {
  --fm-ink: var(--fm-dark-ink);
  --fm-accent: var(--fm-dark-ink);
  --fm-accent-text: var(--fm-dark-ink);
  --fm-callout-color: var(--fm-dark-ink);
  --fm-ink-muted: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-dark-ink) 68%, transparent);
  --fm-border: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-dark-ink) 22%, transparent);
  --fm-surface: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-dark-ink) 5%, transparent);
  --fm-surface-alt: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-dark-ink) 9%, transparent);
  color: var(--fm-dark-ink);
  --fm-info: var(--fm-info-light);
  --fm-success: var(--fm-success-light);
  --fm-warning: var(--fm-warning-light);
  --fm-danger: var(--fm-danger-light);
}

/* ── Full-bleed sections ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The band spans the viewport (its own margins cancel the centred column) and
   then insets its CONTENT back to the column, so text stays aligned with the
   rest of the document while the ground runs edge to edge. */
.fm-band {
  display: block;
  margin: 2.5em var(--fm-bleed-margin);
  --fm-mt: 2.5em;
  --fm-mb: 2.5em;
  padding: 2.5em var(--fm-bleed-pad);
}
.fm-band > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
/* A ticker strip under a masthead is one device, not two: consecutive bands
   sit flush rather than showing the page between them. */
.fm-band + .fm-band { margin-top: 0; }
.fm-band > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fm-cover {
  min-height: min(72vh, 34rem);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  margin-top: -2.5rem;
  container-type: inline-size;
}
/* fill=page: a title page of its own; the report continues on the next. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--fill { break-after: page; }
/* A cover's title is set at its layout's size (--fm-cover-title-size), or
   smaller when its longest word (--fm-title-chars, which the renderer
   stamps) would not fit the title's column at that size: a title word broken
   across two lines reads as a mistake. The column is the cover's own width
   (cqi) unless the layout narrows it (--fm-cover-title-col); 0.62em is a
   generous average glyph for a bold heading face. Both divide by the h1's
   width fit, so a theme's title sets as wide as the default theme's. A
   theme's rule over a heading (its ::after, set in the margin above it)
   would strike the kicker here, where the title has no margin: on a cover
   the heading keeps only the rule under it. */
.fm-cover :is(h1, h2, h3)::after { border-top: none; }
.fm-cover h1 {
  font-size: calc(min(
    var(--fm-cover-title-size, 3em),
    calc(var(--fm-cover-title-col, 100cqi) / (var(--fm-title-chars, 1) * 0.62))
  ) / var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  margin-top: 0;
}
/* Masthead lines: the kicker sits above the title, the dek below a rule. */
.fm-kicker {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: calc(0.75em / var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1));
  line-height: calc(var(--fm-body-leading, 1.55) * var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1));
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  margin-bottom: calc(0.9em * var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1));
}
.fm-dek {
  margin-top: 1em;
  padding-top: calc(0.7em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  border-top: var(--fm-border-width) solid currentColor;
  font-size: 0.95em;
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* ── Cover layouts (layout=) ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The layout is the cover's COMPOSITION; the tone is its ground, so every
   layout works on every tone. Each keeps the masthead lines as DIRECT children
   of the cover (the editor's kicker/dek islands depend on that) and is written
   in em, so the Insert menu's thumbnails shrink it faithfully. Two classes
   outrank a theme's own .fm-cover { text-align } whatever the sheet order. */

.fm-cover.fm-cover--poster h1, .fm-cover.fm-cover--spine h1,
.fm-cover.fm-cover--split h1, .fm-cover.fm-cover--minimal h1,
.fm-cover.fm-cover--block h1 { text-align: left; }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--centered h1, .fm-cover.fm-cover--frame h1 {
  text-align: center;
}

/* Centred: everything on the axis; the sub's rule becomes a short centred bar. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--centered {
  align-items: center;
  text-align: center;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--centered h1 { --fm-cover-title-size: 3.6em; max-width: calc(14em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--centered .fm-dek {
  border-top: none;
  padding-top: 0;
  max-width: 34em;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--centered .fm-dek::before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  width: 3em;
  height: 0.2em;
  margin: 0 auto 1em;
  background: currentColor;
}

/* Poster: an accent bar at the head, the title set huge and pushed to the foot. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--poster {
  justify-content: flex-end;
  text-align: left;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--poster::before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  width: 5em;
  height: 0.6em;
  margin-bottom: auto;
  background: var(--fm-accent);
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--poster h1 {
  --fm-cover-title-size: 4.4em;
  line-height: calc(0.98 * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  max-width: calc(11em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  margin-top: calc(0.4em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--poster .fm-dek { max-width: 40em; }

/* Spine: a bound edge — an accent rule down the whole left side, the text
   hanging off it. The rule sits OUTSIDE the column so the text stays aligned. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--spine {
  text-align: left;
  border-left: 0.6em solid var(--fm-accent);
  padding-left: calc(var(--fm-bleed-pad) - 0.6em);
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--spine .fm-kicker { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--spine .fm-dek {
  border-top: none;
  padding-top: 0;
  border-left: 0.15em solid currentColor;
  padding-left: 1em;
  max-width: 36em;
}

/* Frame: a double hairline rule inset from the edges, the words centred in
   it — the printed report cover. The frame follows the theme's rule weight. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--frame {
  position: relative;
  align-items: center;
  text-align: center;
  padding-block: 4.5em;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--frame::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 1.4em max(1.4em, calc(var(--fm-bleed-pad) - 1.6em));
  border: var(--fm-border-width) solid currentColor;
  outline: var(--fm-border-width) solid currentColor;
  outline-offset: 0.35em;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--frame h1 { max-width: calc(14em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--frame .fm-dek {
  border-top: none;
  padding-top: 0;
  font-size: 0.8em;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  max-width: 34em;
}

/* Split: the kicker across the head, then the title left and the sub right
   on a vertical rule, both at the foot — an editorial spread. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--split {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
  column-gap: 3em;
  align-items: end;
  align-content: space-between;
  text-align: left;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--split .fm-kicker {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  align-self: start;
  margin-bottom: calc(3em * var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1));
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--split h1 {
  grid-column: 1;
  margin: 0;
  --fm-cover-title-size: 3.4em;
  --fm-cover-title-col: calc((100cqi - 3em) * 0.6);
  line-height: calc(1.02 * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--split > p { grid-column: 1; }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--split .fm-dek {
  grid-column: 2;
  margin-top: 0;
  border-top: none;
  padding-top: 0;
  border-left: var(--fm-border-width) solid currentColor;
  padding-left: calc(1.2em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  font-weight: 400;
}

/* Minimal: top-set and quiet — a smaller title, the sub in muted ink, a
   hairline foot instead of a ground. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--minimal {
  justify-content: flex-start;
  text-align: left;
  padding-top: 5em;
  padding-bottom: calc(2.5em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  border-bottom: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--minimal h1 { --fm-cover-title-size: 2.6em; max-width: calc(18em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--minimal .fm-kicker { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--minimal .fm-dek {
  border-top: none;
  padding-top: 0;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  max-width: 36em;
}

/* Block: the title set as a solid block of the accent. On the accent ground
   the block would vanish into it, so that tone keeps the plain title. */
.fm-cover.fm-cover--block { text-align: left; }
.fm-cover.fm-cover--block:not(.fm-tone--accent) h1 {
  align-self: flex-start;
  background: var(--fm-accent-ground);
  color: var(--fm-accent-ground-ink);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: calc(0.18em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)) calc(0.45em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  max-width: calc(14em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  box-decoration-break: clone;
  -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
}
.fm-cover.fm-cover--block .fm-dek { max-width: 36em; }

/* ── Steps: a numbered process list ───────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The numbers are a CSS counter, so the author writes plain paragraphs and
   never renumbers by hand when a step is inserted. */
.fm-steps {
  counter-reset: fm-step;
  margin: 1.6em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.6em;
  --fm-mb: 1.6em;
  border: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  background: var(--fm-surface);
}
.fm-steps > * {
  counter-increment: fm-step;
  position: relative;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1em calc(1.2em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px)) 1em calc(4.2em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fm-border);
}
/* The container's border at the theme's width comes out of the items it
   frames (--fm-border-give): the first item's top, the last item's bottom. */
.fm-steps > :first-child { padding-top: calc(1em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px)); }
.fm-steps > :last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: calc(1em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px)); }
.fm-steps > *::before {
  content: counter(fm-step, decimal-leading-zero);
  position: absolute;
  left: 1.2em;
  top: 1em;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 0.85em;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}

/* ── Numbered sections (report numbering=sections) ────────────────────────── */
/* Only TOP-LEVEL headings are numbered: a heading inside a block is not a
   document section (the format's own rule), so a band or a card can hold one
   without disturbing the sequence. The counters live on the document root,
   which is where readFastrDocumentSettings puts the class. */
.fm-doc--numbered { counter-reset: fm-sec 0; }
.fm-doc--numbered body > .fm-numbered--sec {
  counter-increment: fm-sec;
  counter-reset: fm-sub 0;
}
.fm-doc--numbered body > .fm-numbered--sec::before {
  content: counter(fm-sec) ". ";
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
.fm-doc--numbered body > .fm-numbered--sub { counter-increment: fm-sub; }
.fm-doc--numbered body > .fm-numbered--sub::before {
  content: counter(fm-sec) "." counter(fm-sub) " ";
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}

/* ── Table of contents ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The list is the document's own outline (the renderer fills it in), so the
   only job here is to make it read as a contents page: a quiet panel, the
   levels stepped by indent, the entries as plain ink rather than links. */
.fm-toc {
  display: block;
  margin: 1.6em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.6em;
  --fm-mb: 1.6em;
  padding: calc(1.2em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px)) calc(1.4em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  border: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  background: var(--fm-surface);
}
.fm-toc__title {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--fm-heading-tracking);
  text-transform: var(--fm-heading-case);
  font-size: 0.85em;
  margin-bottom: 0.7em;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
.fm-toc__list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}
.fm-toc__item {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.25em 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fm-border);
}
.fm-toc__item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
/* A long contents list (FASTR_TOC_COLUMNS_FROM entries and more) runs in two
   columns, so the block stays under a page's height. */
.fm-toc__list--columns { columns: 2; column-gap: 2em; }
.fm-toc__list--columns .fm-toc__item { break-inside: avoid; }
.fm-toc__item--2 { padding-left: 1.2em; }
.fm-toc__item--3 { padding-left: 2.4em; font-size: 0.95em; }
.fm-toc__item--4, .fm-toc__item--5, .fm-toc__item--6 {
  padding-left: 3.6em;
  font-size: 0.95em;
}
.fm-toc__item a {
  color: var(--fm-ink);
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: none;
}
.fm-toc__item a:hover { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-toc__empty {
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  font-style: italic;
}

/* A top-level h1 is deliberately NOT special: the title page is :::cover's
   job, and an opening # heading is just a heading. The only concession is
   standard typography — the document's first element drops its top margin.
   :where() keeps the rule at zero specificity so a first-child cover/band
   still wins with its own negative bleed margin. */
body > :where(:first-child) { margin-top: 0; }

/* ── Image backgrounds (resolved from the image registry at render time) ──── */
.fm-has-bgimage {
  position: relative;
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  isolation: isolate;
}
.fm-has-bgimage > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
.fm-overlay::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.fm-overlay--dark::before { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55); }
.fm-overlay--light::before { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72); }

/* ── Figure widths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* small and medium are shares of the column (--fm-fig-share, with the figure
   rules above). width=wide (accepted, still classed fm-figure--wide) once
   overhung the column by up to 4rem a side: on a paged sheet that crosses
   the margin line and reads as a mistake, not a design (Nick, 2026-09-10),
   so it is the column now. width=full bleeds edge to edge, as a band does. */
.fm-figure--full {
  margin: 2em var(--fm-bleed-margin);
}
.fm-figure--full .fm-figure__caption {
  padding-inline: var(--fm-bleed-pad);
}

/* ── Logos (:::logos) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* A row of logos at ONE height: the size sets the row's box, each logo takes
   the height and its own width, so the block's height is known before any
   image has loaded (the page layout measures it straight away). A logo that
   would overflow the row shrinks with its aspect kept. */
.fm-logos {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: 1.6em;
  box-sizing: content-box;
  height: 3em;
  margin: 1.2em 0;
  --fm-mt: 1.2em;
  --fm-mb: 1.2em;
}
.fm-logos--s { height: 2em; }
.fm-logos--l { height: 4.5em; }
.fm-logos--center { justify-content: center; }
.fm-logos--right { justify-content: flex-end; }
.fm-logos--spread { justify-content: space-between; }
.fm-logos > .fm-logo {
  display: block;
  flex: 0 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  width: auto;
  max-width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  margin: 0;
  object-fit: contain;
}
.fm-logos.fm-tone, .fm-logos.fm-has-bg, .fm-logos.fm-has-bgimage {
  padding: 0.9em 1.1em;
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
}
.fm-tiles .fm-logos, .fm-columns .fm-logos { margin: 0; }

/* ── Page templates (:::page) ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-tpl {
  display: grid;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 245mm) - 8px);
  margin: 0;
  --fm-mt: 0;
  --fm-mb: 0;
  padding: var(--fm-tpl-pad, 0);
  gap: 1.2em 2em;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  align-content: start;
  overflow: hidden;
  position: relative;
}
/* A ground needs room inside it where no page is painted under it (the .html
   export); the editor and print paint the whole sheet and zero this. */
.fm-tpl.fm-tone, .fm-tpl.fm-has-bg, .fm-tpl.fm-has-bgimage {
  --fm-tpl-pad: 2em;
}
.fm-tpl > * { min-width: 0; min-height: 0; overflow: hidden; margin: 0; }
.fm-tpl-main > :first-child, .fm-tpl-slot > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
.fm-tpl-main > :last-child, .fm-tpl-slot > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fm-tpl > .fm-kicker { grid-area: kicker; margin: 0; }
.fm-tpl-main { grid-area: main; }
.fm-tpl-slot--media { grid-area: media; }
.fm-tpl-slot--empty { display: none; }
.fm-tpl-slot .fm-figure { margin: 0; }
.fm-tpl-slot .fm-figure__caption { font-size: calc(0.75em / var(--fm-fit-caption, 1)); }
.fm-tpl-slot__title {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1.05em;
  margin-bottom: 0.7em;
}
.fm-tpl-slot__label {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: 0.75em;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--fm-ink-muted);
  margin-bottom: 0.6em;
}
/* Stats in a template are the layout's, not tiles: no panel of their own. */
.fm-tpl-slot > .fm-stat {
  margin: 0;
  background: none;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  box-shadow: none;
}
/* A photo is the area's, not a framed figure. */
.fm-tpl-slot--media .fm-figure {
  border: none;
  padding: 0;
  background: none;
  box-shadow: none;
  border-radius: 0;
}

/* story: the headline in a gutter column beside a rule, the prose to its
   right, a photo across the page. */
.fm-tpl--story {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas:
    ".      main"
    "kicker main"
    "side   main"
    ".      main"
    "media  media";
  column-gap: 0;
  row-gap: 0;
}
.fm-tpl--story.fm-tpl--media-top {
  grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas:
    "media  media"
    ".      main"
    "kicker main"
    "side   main"
    ".      main";
}
.fm-tpl--story > .fm-kicker { padding-right: calc(1.6em * var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1)); color: var(--fm-ink); }
.fm-tpl--story .fm-tpl-slot--side { grid-area: side; padding-right: 1.6em; }
.fm-tpl--story .fm-tpl-slot--side::before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  height: 0.45em;
  width: 80%;
  background: var(--fm-accent);
  margin-bottom: 0.9em;
}
.fm-tpl--story .fm-tpl-slot--side :is(h1, h2, h3) {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
  line-height: calc(1.15 * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
}
.fm-tpl--story .fm-tpl-main {
  border-left: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-accent);
  padding: 1.5em 0 1.5em calc(1.8em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  align-self: stretch;
}
.fm-tpl--story .fm-tpl-slot--media { margin-top: 1.4em; }
.fm-tpl--story.fm-tpl--media-top .fm-tpl-slot--media { margin: 0 0 1.4em; }
.fm-tpl--story .fm-tpl-slot--media img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: none;
  height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 245mm) * 0.4);
  max-height: none;
  object-fit: cover;
}

/* summary: a heading and standfirst, the headline totals under gradient
   caps, a heavy rule, then the breakdown on heavy bars. The headline totals
   are set at hero size in the middle of the page and the breakdown stands on
   its foot, so the space between them is the layout's, not a page left
   unfinished. */
.fm-tpl--summary {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(min-content, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "headline" "breakdown";
  row-gap: 1.8em;
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-main {
  border-top: 0.2em solid var(--fm-accent);
  padding-top: 1em;
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0 0 calc(0.4em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline {
  grid-area: headline;
  display: grid;
  grid-auto-flow: column;
  grid-auto-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  align-content: center;
  gap: 1em;
  text-align: center;
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline > .fm-stat::before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  height: 1.1em;
  margin-bottom: 1em;
  border-radius: min(var(--fm-radius), 0.3em);
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent-ground) 70%, var(--fm-page)), var(--fm-accent-ground));
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline > .fm-stat:nth-child(2)::before {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--fm-accent-ground), color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent-ground) 55%, var(--fm-ink-ground)));
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline > .fm-stat:nth-child(3)::before {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent-ground) 55%, var(--fm-ink-ground)), var(--fm-ink-ground));
}
/* Hero size, but never wider than its column: a stat is its own container,
   so a longer value sets smaller rather than running into its neighbour. */
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline > .fm-stat { container-type: inline-size; }
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline .fm-stat__value { font-size: calc(min(4.8em, 25cqi) / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1)); white-space: nowrap; }
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--headline .fm-stat__label {
  font-weight: 700;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--fm-ink);
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--breakdown {
  grid-area: breakdown;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
  align-content: start;
  gap: 1.6em 1.2em;
  border-top: 0.7em solid var(--fm-ink-ground);
  padding-top: 1.2em;
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--breakdown > .fm-tpl-slot__title { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin: 0; }
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--breakdown > .fm-stat {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  border-bottom: 0.5em solid var(--fm-ink);
  padding-bottom: 0.5em;
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--breakdown .fm-stat__label {
  order: -1;
  margin: 0 0 calc(0.35em * var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
  padding-bottom: calc(0.3em * var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1) - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  border-bottom: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--fm-ink);
}
.fm-tpl--summary .fm-tpl-slot--breakdown .fm-stat__value { font-size: calc(2.1em / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1)); color: var(--fm-ink); }

/* findings: numbered findings in two columns, the number warm when the
   finding's lead is marked as bad news. The rows share what the page has
   left over, so the findings stand on a grid down to its foot rather than
   all at its top; a row is never shorter than its findings (a track of
   minmax(0, 1fr) clipped a long one under the next row's rule), and
   findings that need more than the page run past it, which the page map
   reports as OVERFULL. */
.fm-tpl--findings {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "items";
  row-gap: 1.6em;
}
.fm-tpl--findings > .fm-kicker { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-tpl--findings .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0; font-size: calc(2em / var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--findings .fm-tpl-slot--items {
  grid-area: items;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  grid-auto-rows: minmax(min-content, 1fr);
  gap: 2.4em 2.4em;
  font-size: 1.12em;
  counter-reset: fm-finding;
}
.fm-tpl--findings .fm-tpl-slot--items > p {
  margin: 0;
  counter-increment: fm-finding;
  border-top: 0.15em solid var(--fm-ink);
  padding-top: 0.6em;
}
.fm-tpl--findings .fm-tpl-slot--items > p::before {
  content: counter(fm-finding);
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  font-size: 2.8em;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-bottom: 0.15em;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
.fm-tpl--findings .fm-tpl-slot--items > p:has(.fm-mark--danger)::before { color: var(--fm-danger); }
.fm-tpl--findings .fm-tpl-slot--items > p > strong:first-child {
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: 1.12em;
  margin-bottom: 0.3em;
}

/* exec: the headline numbers stacked in a sidebar on a ground, the summary
   and its next steps beside them. */
.fm-tpl--exec {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "side kicker" "side main";
  column-gap: 2.2em;
  row-gap: 0;
}
.fm-tpl--exec > .fm-kicker { color: var(--fm-accent-text); margin-bottom: calc(0.6em * var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1)); }
/* A slot on a ground (tone=) is an inset panel: the theme's corners, as
   every other panel in the report has. */
.fm-tpl-slot.fm-tone { border-radius: var(--fm-radius); }
.fm-tpl--exec .fm-tpl-slot--side {
  grid-area: side;
  padding: 2em 1.6em;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 2.2em;
}
.fm-tpl--exec .fm-tpl-slot--side .fm-stat__value { font-size: calc(2.8em / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1)); color: inherit; }
.fm-tpl--exec .fm-tpl-slot--side .fm-stat__label { color: inherit; opacity: 0.85; }
.fm-tpl--exec .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin-top: 0; }

/* opener: a large section number, the title and a line or two; an optional
   photo across the foot. */
.fm-tpl--opener {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas: "number" "main" "." "media";
  row-gap: 1em;
}
.fm-tpl--opener .fm-tpl__number {
  grid-area: number;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  font-size: 9em;
  line-height: 0.9;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
  margin-top: 0.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--opener .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { font-size: calc(3.2em / var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); margin: 0 0 calc(0.3em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); line-height: calc(1.05 * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--opener .fm-tpl-main p { font-size: 1.2em; max-width: 30em; }
.fm-tpl--opener .fm-tpl-slot--media img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: none;
  height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 245mm) * 0.32);
  max-height: none;
  object-fit: cover;
}
.fm-tpl:not(.fm-tpl--opener) .fm-tpl__number { display: none; }

/* back: everything at the foot of the page under an accent rule. */
.fm-tpl--back {
  grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "." "main";
}
.fm-tpl--back::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: var(--fm-tpl-pad, 0);
  left: var(--fm-tpl-pad, 0);
  width: 30%;
  height: 0.25em;
  background: var(--fm-accent);
}
.fm-tpl--back .fm-tpl-main {
  font-size: 0.9em;
  border-top: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
  padding-top: calc(1.2em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
}
.fm-tpl--back .fm-tpl-main .fm-logos { margin: 0 0 1.4em; }
.fm-tpl--back .fm-tpl-main p:last-child { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--fm-ink-muted); }

/* boxed: two columns of running prose over a boxed aside and its notes. */
.fm-tpl--boxed {
  grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto;
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "box" "notes";
  row-gap: 1.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--boxed .fm-tpl-main { column-count: 2; column-gap: 1.8em; }
.fm-tpl--boxed .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2, h3) { column-span: all; margin-top: 0; color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-tpl--boxed .fm-tpl-slot--box {
  grid-area: box;
  background: var(--fm-surface-alt);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: 1.4em 1.6em;
  column-count: 2;
  column-gap: 1.8em;
  font-size: 0.92em;
}
.fm-tpl--boxed .fm-tpl-slot--box > .fm-tpl-slot__title {
  column-span: all;
  padding-bottom: calc(0.5em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  border-bottom: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
}
.fm-tpl--boxed .fm-tpl-slot--notes { grid-area: notes; font-size: 0.78em; color: var(--fm-ink-muted); }

/* targets: a board of cards, each goal's figure set large, a rule and where
   the country stands today at its foot. */
.fm-tpl--targets {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "cards";
  row-gap: 1.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--targets .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0 0 calc(0.3em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); font-size: calc(2.2em / var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--targets .fm-tpl-slot--cards {
  grid-area: cards;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  grid-auto-rows: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 0.9em;
}
.fm-tpl--targets .fm-card {
  margin: 0;
  background: none;
  border: 0.1em solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 70%, transparent);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  font-size: 0.9em;
}
.fm-tpl--targets .fm-card__title {
  font-size: calc(0.85em / var(--fm-fit-card-title, 1));
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.fm-tpl--targets .fm-card p strong {
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: 2em;
  line-height: 1.05;
}
.fm-card__progress {
  margin-top: auto;
  padding-top: 0.6em;
}
.fm-card__progress-label {
  font-size: 0.72em;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  border-bottom: var(--fm-border-width) solid currentColor;
  padding-bottom: calc(0.25em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
}
.fm-card__progress-value {
  text-align: right;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  font-size: 1.3em;
  margin-top: 0.15em;
}

/* compare: two halves on contrasting grounds, the change on the seam. Each
   half's few lines sit centred on its ground, level with the change, so the
   grounds read as a poster rather than a page stopped half way. Both halves
   clear the disc on the seam. */
.fm-tpl--compare {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker kicker" "main main" "left right";
  column-gap: 0;
  row-gap: 1.2em;
}
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin-top: 0; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--left { grid-area: left; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--right { grid-area: right; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--left, .fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--right {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  padding: 2.4em 2em;
}
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--left { padding-right: 3.4em; }
/* The halves meet at the seam: only their outer corners round. */
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--left.fm-tone { border-radius: var(--fm-radius) 0 0 var(--fm-radius); }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--right.fm-tone { border-radius: 0 var(--fm-radius) var(--fm-radius) 0; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot--right { padding-left: 3.4em; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot .fm-stat__value { font-size: calc(4.2em / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1)); color: inherit; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot .fm-stat__label { color: inherit; font-size: calc(1em / var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1)); margin-bottom: calc(1.2em * var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl-slot .fm-tpl-slot__label { color: inherit; opacity: 0.8; }
.fm-tpl--compare .fm-tpl__delta {
  position: absolute;
  left: 50%;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  z-index: 1;
  width: 5.6em;
  height: 5.6em;
  border-radius: calc(var(--fm-radius) * 999);
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  background: var(--fm-page);
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  font-size: 1.1em;
  box-shadow: 0 0.1em 0.5em color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-ink) 25%, transparent);
}
.fm-tpl:not(.fm-tpl--compare) .fm-tpl__delta { display: none; }

/* timeline: milestones alternating either side of a spine, spread down
   its whole length. */
.fm-tpl--timeline {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "events";
  row-gap: 1.6em;
}
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0; }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events {
  grid-area: events;
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 1.4em;
  font-size: 1.1em;
}
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: calc(50% - 0.1em);
  top: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  width: 0.2em;
  background: var(--fm-accent);
}
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p { position: relative; margin: 0; width: 44%; }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p:nth-child(odd) { text-align: right; }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p:nth-child(even) { margin-left: 56%; }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: 0.3em;
  width: 0.9em;
  height: 0.9em;
  border-radius: calc(var(--fm-radius) * 999);
  background: var(--fm-accent);
  border: 0.2em solid var(--fm-page);
}
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p:nth-child(odd)::after { right: calc(-6% / 0.44 - 0.65em); }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p:nth-child(even)::after { left: calc(-6% / 0.44 - 0.65em); }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p:has(.fm-mark--danger)::after { background: var(--fm-danger); }
.fm-tpl--timeline .fm-tpl-slot--events > p > strong:first-child {
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}

/* voices: a photo, a pull quote on a card over its lower edge, context. */
.fm-tpl--voices {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "media" "quote" "main";
  row-gap: 0;
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--media img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: none;
  height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 245mm) * 0.5);
  max-height: none;
  object-fit: cover;
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--quote {
  grid-area: quote;
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  margin: -4.5em 7% 1.6em;
  padding: 1.6em 1.8em 1.4em;
  background: var(--fm-page);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-size: 1.35em;
  line-height: 1.3;
  box-shadow: 0 0.1em 0.6em color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-ink) 18%, transparent);
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--empty + .fm-tpl-slot--quote,
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--quote:first-child {
  margin-top: 0;
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--quote::before {
  content: "\201C";
  display: block;
  font-size: 2.6em;
  line-height: 0.6;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--quote > p {
  font-size: calc(1em / var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
  line-height: calc(1.3 * var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--quote .fm-quote__cite {
  display: block;
  margin-top: calc(0.8em * var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  font-size: calc(0.55em / var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  line-height: calc(1.3 * var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  font-style: normal;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-slot--media .fm-figure__caption { display: none; }
.fm-tpl--voices .fm-tpl-main { max-width: 34em; }

/* spotlight: the prose in a column; beside it a short paragraph, then a
   panel (the portrait and the quote, both on the accent ground) running to
   the sheet's right edge. The template reaches the edge through the bleed
   margin, and the right column's padding brings its text back to the
   measure, as a band does. */
.fm-tpl--spotlight {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "main top" "main media" "main quote";
  column-gap: 2.2em;
  row-gap: 0;
  margin-right: var(--fm-bleed-margin);
  --fm-tpl-fill: main;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin-top: 0; }
/* The panel starts a fifth of the way down at least, as a short paragraph
   above it would otherwise lift it to the top and leave its foot empty. */
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--top {
  grid-area: top;
  min-height: calc(var(--fm-page-area, 245mm) * 0.2);
  box-sizing: border-box;
  padding: 0 var(--fm-bleed-pad) 2em 0;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--media {
  padding: 2.6em var(--fm-bleed-pad) 0 2.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--media img {
  display: block;
  width: 64%;
  max-width: none;
  height: auto;
  max-height: none;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  margin: 0 auto;
  border-radius: calc(var(--fm-radius) * 999);
  object-fit: cover;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--media .fm-figure__caption { display: none; }
/* The editor's Add photo box, where the portrait will stand: a dashed
   circle inside the panel, which stays one ground. */
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--empty.fm-tpl-slot--media {
  min-height: 0;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--empty.fm-tpl-slot--media::after {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 64%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  border: 2px dashed currentColor;
  border-radius: calc(var(--fm-radius) * 999);
  opacity: 0.85;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--quote {
  grid-area: quote;
  padding: 2.4em var(--fm-bleed-pad) 2.4em 2.4em;
  font-family: var(--fm-font-heading);
  font-weight: var(--fm-heading-weight);
  font-size: 1.5em;
  line-height: 1.25;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--quote::before {
  content: "\201C";
  display: block;
  font-size: 2.2em;
  line-height: 0.7;
  margin-bottom: 0.1em;
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--quote > p {
  font-size: calc(1em / var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
  line-height: calc(1.25 * var(--fm-fit-quote, 1));
}
.fm-tpl--spotlight .fm-tpl-slot--quote .fm-quote__cite {
  display: block;
  margin-top: calc(1.2em * var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  font-family: var(--fm-font-body);
  font-size: calc(0.55em / var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: calc(1.4 * var(--fm-fit-cite, 1));
}

/* feature: the heading, a bold lead and the prose in a column; the photo
   fills the rest of the page, out to the sheet's right edge. */
.fm-tpl--feature {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker media" "main media";
  column-gap: 2.4em;
  row-gap: 0;
  margin-right: var(--fm-bleed-margin);
  --fm-tpl-fill: main;
}
.fm-tpl--feature > .fm-kicker { margin-bottom: calc(0.8em * var(--fm-fit-kicker, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--feature .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin-top: 0; }
.fm-tpl--feature .fm-tpl-slot--media .fm-figure { height: 100%; }
.fm-tpl--feature .fm-tpl-slot--media img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: none;
  height: 100%;
  max-height: none;
  object-fit: cover;
}
.fm-tpl--feature .fm-tpl-slot--media .fm-figure__caption { display: none; }

/* profile: a map and a column of facts under the district's name. */
.fm-tpl--profile {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker kicker" "main main" "map facts";
  row-gap: 1.2em;
}
.fm-tpl--profile > .fm-kicker { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) {
  margin: 0 0 calc(0.4em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  font-size: calc(2.4em / var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  padding-bottom: calc(0.3em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1));
  border-bottom: calc(0.08em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)) solid var(--fm-ink);
}
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--map { grid-area: map; }
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--map img { width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--facts {
  grid-area: facts;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--facts > .fm-stat {
  border-bottom: var(--fm-border-width) solid var(--fm-border);
  padding-bottom: calc(0.7em - var(--fm-border-give, 0px));
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--facts .fm-stat__label {
  order: -1;
  margin: 0 0 calc(0.2em * var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
  font-size: calc(0.72em / var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--facts .fm-stat__value { font-size: calc(2.4em / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--profile .fm-tpl-slot--facts .fm-stat__delta { align-self: flex-start; }

/* method: short panels in a grid, the citation at the foot. */
.fm-tpl--method {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "panels" "cite";
  row-gap: 1.4em;
  --fm-tpl-fill: panels;
}
.fm-tpl--method .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0; }
.fm-tpl--method .fm-tpl-slot--panels {
  grid-area: panels;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  align-content: start;
  gap: 1.8em 2.2em;
}
.fm-tpl--method .fm-card { margin: 0; background: none; border: none; padding: 0; font-size: 0.95em; }
.fm-tpl--method .fm-card__title { font-size: calc(1.1em / var(--fm-fit-card-title, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--method .fm-tpl-slot--cite {
  grid-area: cite;
  background: var(--fm-page);
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  padding: 1.1em 1.3em;
  font-size: 0.88em;
}

/* ladder: results stacked as full-width bars stepping from the accent to
   the ink, each with an icon disc rising from its foot. */
.fm-tpl--ladder {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "rows";
  row-gap: 1.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--ladder > .fm-kicker { color: var(--fm-accent-text); }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-main {
  border-bottom: 0.25em solid var(--fm-accent);
  padding-bottom: 0.8em;
}
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0 0 calc(0.3em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); text-transform: uppercase; }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows {
  grid-area: rows;
  display: grid;
  grid-auto-rows: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 0.4em;
}
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows > .fm-stat {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 24% minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr);
  grid-template-areas: "icon value label";
  align-items: center;
  column-gap: 1.2em;
  padding: 0 1.4em 0 0;
  border-radius: var(--fm-radius);
  color: var(--fm-ink-ground-ink);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-accent-ground) var(--fm-rung, 100%), var(--fm-ink-ground));
}
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows > .fm-stat:nth-child(2) { --fm-rung: 78%; }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows > .fm-stat:nth-child(3) { --fm-rung: 56%; }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows > .fm-stat:nth-child(4) { --fm-rung: 34%; }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows > .fm-stat:nth-child(5) { --fm-rung: 14%; }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows > .fm-stat:nth-child(6) { --fm-rung: 0%; }
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows .fm-icon {
  grid-area: icon;
  align-self: end;
  justify-self: center;
  width: 3.6em;
  height: 3.6em;
  margin: 0 0 -0.6em;
  padding: 0.9em;
  border-radius: calc(var(--fm-radius) * 999);
  box-sizing: content-box;
  color: var(--fm-ink-ground);
  background: var(--fm-page);
  -webkit-mask: none;
  mask: none;
  position: relative;
}
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows .fm-icon::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0.9em;
  background: currentColor;
  -webkit-mask: var(--fm-icon) center / contain no-repeat;
  mask: var(--fm-icon) center / contain no-repeat;
}
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows .fm-stat__value {
  grid-area: value;
  font-size: calc(3em / var(--fm-fit-stat-value, 1));
  text-align: right;
  color: inherit;
}
.fm-tpl--ladder .fm-tpl-slot--rows .fm-stat__label {
  grid-area: label;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: calc(0.95em / var(--fm-fit-stat-label, 1));
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  color: inherit;
}

/* scorecard: a table whose cells fill with the status their mark names. The
   table takes the page down to the notes, its rows sharing the height. */
.fm-tpl--scorecard {
  grid-template-rows: auto auto minmax(min-content, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas: "kicker" "main" "table" "notes";
  row-gap: 1.2em;
}
.fm-tpl--scorecard .fm-tpl-main :is(h1, h2) { margin: 0 0 calc(0.3em * var(--fm-h-fit, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard .fm-tpl-slot--table { grid-area: table; }
.fm-tpl--scorecard .fm-tpl-slot--notes { grid-area: notes; font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--fm-ink-muted); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard table { width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0.2em; font-size: 1.1em; }
.fm-tpl--scorecard td, .fm-tpl--scorecard th { padding: 0.55em 0.7em; border: none; vertical-align: middle; }
.fm-tpl--scorecard th { padding: calc(0.55em * var(--fm-fit-th, 1)) calc(0.7em * var(--fm-fit-th, 1)); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard td:has(> .fm-mark--success) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-success) 22%, transparent); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard td:has(> .fm-mark--warning) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-warning) 22%, transparent); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard td:has(> .fm-mark--danger) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-danger) 22%, transparent); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard td:has(> .fm-mark--info) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fm-info) 22%, transparent); }
.fm-tpl--scorecard td > .fm-mark { font-weight: 700; }

/* ── Icons (icon= on a stat or a card) ────────────────────────────────────── */
.fm-icon {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 1.6em;
  height: 1.6em;
  background: currentColor;
  -webkit-mask: var(--fm-icon) center / contain no-repeat;
  mask: var(--fm-icon) center / contain no-repeat;
}
.fm-stat > .fm-icon, .fm-card > .fm-icon {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 0.5em;
  color: var(--fm-accent-text);
}
